      "formation": "[Noun] + なら\n[Verb Plain Form] + なら\n[い-adj / な-adj] + なら",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "〜なら takes up a topic or condition raised by the other speaker or the situation, and provides advice, suggestions, or requests (e.g. 日本の温泉に行くなら、箱根がおすすめですよ = If you are going to a Japanese hot spring, Hakone is my recommendation). Unlike 〜たら, 〜なら does NOT require the condition to happen first chronologically; the action in the main clause can happen BEFORE the condition (e.g. 日本へ行くなら、カメラを買ったほうがいい = If you are going to Japan, you should buy a camera [before you go]).",
