    },
    "titleMy": "日本留学二年目に見られた変化 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "日本留学二年目に見られた変化 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "Two years have already swiftly passed since I came to study abroad in Japan from Myanmar. When I first arrived in Japan, I could not speak Japanese well, and even shopping at the supermarket was a continuous source of nervous tension. Moreover, due to cultural and habitual differences, I became homesick, doing nothing but calling my family in my home country at night.\n\nHowever, continuing to study daily at the Japanese language school and gaining experience through part-time jobs, my life changed tremendously. Now, I have become able to enjoy everyday conversations with Japanese people without using a dictionary, and no longer get lost even when looking at complicated train route maps. Natto and sashimi, whose smell I disliked at first, I have also become able to eat deliciously.\n\nOn the other hand, some things also ceased. Previously, I chatted late every day with friends back home, but to maintain a disciplined lifestyle, I stopped staying up late. Furthermore, I used to translate all Japanese notices into English to read them, but now I can read Japanese signs and announcements directly, and no longer rely on English.\n\nCompared to myself two years ago, I truly feel my own personal growth. I want to continue striving without giving up and become able to do even more things in the future."
