      "meaning": "Contrasting Japanese Conditionals (Topic/advice, sequence, hypothetical, natural result)",
      "formation": "〜なら: Topic picked from context; advice/suggestions permitted; non-chronological.\n〜たら: Chronological sequence (Once A finishes, then B); general everyday conditional.\n〜ば: Hypothetical condition (If A, then B); focus on prerequisite condition.\n〜と: Natural inevitable result, automatic consequence, or factual discovery (No volition/request in B).",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Mastering the 4 conditional forms is an essential N4 milestone:\n1. 〜と: Inevitable physical result (春になると花が咲く; このボタンを押すと切符が出る). Main clause CANNOT be advice, request, or intention.\n2. 〜たら: General time/hypothetical sequence (家に着いたら電話して). Action A must happen first.\n3. 〜ば: Formal hypothetical or general condition (安ければ買う; 練習すれば上手になる).\n4. 〜なら: Topic condition picking up what the other speaker said, giving advice (美味しいラーメンなら、駅前の店がいいですよ).",
