    "titleMyanmar": "N4修了の振り返りと新たな挑戦 (Reflecting on N4 Completion and New Challenges) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "From when I started studying Japanese until today, I have steadily progressed step by step from N5 to N4. At first, merely memorizing hiragana and basic greetings took all my effort, but now I have become able to differentiate and use advanced patterns like the passive voice, causative forms, giving and receiving verbs, and honorifics according to circumstances.\n\nEspecially when I understood the nuanced differences among conjectures and reports such as 〜らしい, 〜ようだ, and 〜そうだ, I was deeply moved by the richness of Japanese expression. Furthermore, by learning to distinguish 〜ために (expressing conscious purpose) from 〜ように (aiming at natural results or abilities), sentence construction that had once been vague became surprisingly clear.\n\nOf course, midway through there were times when I wrestled with grammatical complexity or felt overwhelmed by the sheer number of kanji. However, thanks to the teachers who earnestly gave me advice and classmates who encouraged one another, I was able to overcome all difficulties. Now having completely mastered N4, facing our new challenge toward the higher peak of N3, I hold immense confidence and hope in my heart."
